(1844,"1844","I","Electric telegraph","Samuel Morse, Alfred Vail; United States","Morse sent the first long-distance message, from Washington to Baltimore, building on earlier British systems. Messages began to outrun any messenger, and the first lasting transatlantic cable in 1866 linked two continents."),
