(1847,"1847–67","L","Handwashing and antisepsis","Ignaz Semmelweis, Joseph Lister","Semmelweis sharply cut deaths from childbed fever in a Vienna hospital ward by having doctors wash with chlorinated lime. Lister later applied carbolic acid to wounds and instruments. Surgery moved from a last resort toward a controlled procedure."),
