(1856,"1856","C","Synthetic dye","William Perkin; London","Aged 18, Perkin accidentally made the purple dye mauveine while trying to synthesize quinine from coal tar. He built a factory to produce it, and the dye and drug industries grew from the same chemistry."),
(1859,"1859","P","Spectroscopy","Gustav Kirchhoff, Robert Bunsen; Heidelberg","Each chemical element emits and absorbs light at its own set of wavelengths. Chemists used this to find new elements, and astronomers began reading the composition of the Sun and stars from their light."),
